WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.010
- I have a very distinct memory
of like being 10 years old,

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.380
and I tried to talk to other kids my age,

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.430
and it did not go well.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.797
I like started making animal noises.

00:00:11.054 --> 00:00:13.618
(blowing sound)

00:00:13.618 --> 00:00:16.701
(happy string music)

00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:20.887
- I don't know that you can say like one,

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:22.170
one thing.
- It's different for everyone.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.010
- Personally for me

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.210
like I was taught by my parents.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.610
So it was literally school at home.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.090
- Homeschooling is where
your house is your school.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.960
- Really depends on what you wanna learn

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.186
and how you want to learn it.

00:00:34.186 --> 00:00:36.010
(happy string music)

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:37.190
- Yes.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.240
- Yeah, I think even if you
don't know that you're awkward

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.450
a lot of times homeschool
people end up being very-

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:44.370
- You are.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:47.620
- I think it depends, 'cause
like you don't seem awkward.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:48.533
I'm awkward.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.330
But like I don't know if that's
because I was homeschooled

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.610
or just because I'm awkward.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:53.473
- Oh of course.

00:00:54.484 --> 00:00:55.317
- Definitely.

00:00:55.317 --> 00:00:56.150
- Yeah.

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:56.983
- Oh my God.

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:01.010
- Homeschooling is really
good because it allows kids

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.220
to learn at their own pace.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.410
I have learning disabilities,

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.460
and I just needed a little
extra time to catch up.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.510
- Everyday is a field trip.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:07.460
Let's go to a museum

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.450
or let's go to the movies.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.590
- Oh I went to a cadaver lab.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.340
Don't most people do that probably?

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:14.031
No?

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.240
No we didn't do the dissecting,

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.920
but we did look at a
body that was dissected,

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:20.470
and they showed us like a brain

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:22.140
and they showed us some testicles

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.230
and they showed us like layers of fat

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.140
to show like what fat
looks like on the inside

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.340
and that freaked me out.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:30.160
- Because there's so much freedom

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.770
there is sometimes more of an opportunity

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:33.810
for it to go wrong.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:36.423
- Basically my parents
aren't great at math.

00:01:37.283 --> 00:01:38.660
Who needs math?

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.855
- I didn't have any
friends 'til I was like 14.

00:01:40.855 --> 00:01:42.020
- So I didn't get friends
'til I was like 19.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:43.603
I was like way older.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:47.920
- Homeschoolers definitely sleep longer

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.170
than public schoolers.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.980
- Depends what dope activity my mom

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.440
or dad had planned for us.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.700
- My homeschooling was not
like most regular homeschoolers

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.050
because I grew up Muslim.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.800
We had a more structural schedule.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.120
You had to wake up at
five for your prayer.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.440
Yeah, you had to wake up for prayer,

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:06.273
and then after prayer

00:02:06.273 --> 00:02:08.570
you had to make sure you
got breakfast before seven,

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:11.253
and then we did martial
arts after meditation time.

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:15.410
- I was never lonely.

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:17.940
There were plenty of
kids in my neighborhood.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.300
There were plenty of other
homeschool families that I knew.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.960
- I wouldn't say it makes you lonely,

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.210
but I would say it makes
you more of a loner.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.950
- I wouldn't say
homeschoolers are any smarter

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.040
than public or private or whatever.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.970
- Homeschoolers are
typically really passionate

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:36.010
about like a smaller number of things,

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.910
and they're really good at those things.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.150
- I wouldn't say I'm book smart.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:42.073
So we're smarter in the
aspect of being an adult.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:47.100
- I was homeschooled all the
way up until I started college,

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.090
and I took like the SATs
just like anyone else.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.930
- We're like a really
good entrance I'd say.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:53.800
Bribery.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.730
- I didn't find success
by going to college.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.480
I just found it doing my own thing.

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:01.830
- My parents are very anti-establishment,

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:02.663
anti-government.

00:03:02.663 --> 00:03:05.300
They wanted to teach us
what they wanted to teach us

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.710
without being told like this
is what your kid's gonna learn.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.140
- It could depend on like
what your learning pace is,

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:13.100
where your like cultural or
like religious beliefs are

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.370
or if you just don't like
the schools in your area.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.830
- Honestly most of the
time it's just because

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.790
your parents wanted you
to learn things at home

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.463
and learn things a different way.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.430
- Homeschoolers are super normal.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.263
- Yeah.

00:03:28.236 --> 00:03:31.319
(happy guitar music)

00:03:33.692 --> 00:03:36.004
(blowing sound)

